WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.911
Week 8: Family, Description, and Possession. describe people and relationships express possession identify a person precisely

2
00:00:08.911 --> 00:00:16.479
Form and meaning. Adjective agreement and position; possessive adjectives and pronouns; tener; personal a.

3
00:00:16.479 --> 00:00:40.966
Model set. Mi hermana mayor es muy amable. Conozco a los padres de Elena. Nuestra familia vive en tres ciudades. ¿Es suyo este retrato? Tengo dos hermanos y una prima. My older sister is very kind. I know Elena's parents. Our family lives in three cities. Is this portrait yours? I have two brothers and one female cousin.

4
00:00:40.966 --> 00:00:51.245
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:51.245 --> 00:01:04.938
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: describe people and relationships; express possession; identify a person precisely. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:04.938 --> 00:01:19.804
Adjectives agree. A variable adjective matches the noun in gender and number: un amigo alto, una amiga alta, unos amigos altos, unas amigas altas. The noun controls the form of the adjective.

7
00:01:19.804 --> 00:01:35.758
Not every adjective changes for gender. Adjectives ending in -e or many consonants commonly keep one singular form: un amigo amable and una amiga amable. They still change for plural number: amigos amables, amigas amables.

8
00:01:35.758 --> 00:01:51.352
Position affects emphasis. Descriptive adjectives usually follow the noun. Some common adjectives can appear before it, sometimes with a change in emphasis or form. First secure agreement; then learn position as part of each expression.

9
00:01:51.352 --> 00:02:16.458
Model language. Mi hermana mayor es muy amable. — My older sister is very kind. Conozco a los padres de Elena. — I know Elena's parents. Nuestra familia vive en tres ciudades. — Our family lives in three cities. ¿Es suyo este retrato? — Is this portrait yours? Tengo dos hermanos y una prima. — I have two brothers and one female cousin.

10
00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:26.463
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
